  "title": "Time, days & months",
  "goal": "Tell and ask the time, name the days and months, and talk about today, yesterday, tomorrow and parts of the day.",
  "intro": "Telugu tells the time in *గంటలు* (gaṇṭalu, hours, literally 'bells') with handy words for quarters and halves: *మూడుంబావు* (quarter past three), *మూడున్నర* (half past three). Note the special form for one o'clock: *ఒంటి గంట* (oṇṭi gaṇṭa).\n\nDays of the week are named after the planets (*సోమ*, moon; *మంగళ*, Mars...) and all end in *-వారం* (vāram). For months, the English names are used in daily life.",
